  "reason": "The existing evidence shows that the RNA-only baseline (config_001) achieves 48.5% validation accuracy, but it's unclear if multimodal approaches could improve this. This experiment tests a multimodal model (model_setting=multimodal) with the same RNA encoder (pca_n2000) as the baseline, paired with resnet50 image encoder and simple concatenation fusion. This directly compares the baseline RNA-only model with a multimodal approach, isolating the effect of adding image data. It addresses the key uncertainty about whether multimodal integration provides performance benefits without introducing other confounding factors like complex aggregation methods."
}

